# The layout of a drawn face with large eyes: the avatar face with the ranges its drawn sheets need
law avatar_face_stylised
kind proportion
derive avatar_face face.law
claim the face of avatar_face, with the ranges of drawn sheets (n=2) where the sheets were measured; every other parameter keeps the range of avatar_face
claim a measured range = each sheet's value with its measurement ± (pixel picks on the sheet's front face, in its own chin-to-eye units), rounded outward to 2 decimals; the calibration floor of picks against 3D bodies is in body units and is not added here; the default is the sheets' mean rounded to 2 decimals
claim eye_height and brow_y are measured on one sheet (the other's brows are under the fringe), mouth_y on both: two sheets are a floor for the range, not its envelope
param eye_height number = 0.52 range 0.45 0.59
param brow_y number = 1.4 range 1.3 1.5
param mouth_y number = 0.37 range 0.26 0.47
